00:35:27,272 --> 00:35:33,272
Is It College Yet?

13
00:38:24,545 --> 00:38:30,545
is a 2002 American animated comedy-drama television film written by Glenn
Eichler and Peggy Nicoll, and directed by Karen Disher.

14
00:41:21,818 --> 00:41:27,818
The film was the second film-length installment of MTV's animated series Daria, after 2000's Is it Fall Yet?, and
served as the series finale, chronicling the end of high school as the characters prepare for college.

15
00:44:19,090 --> 00:44:25,090
Is It College Yet?

16
00:47:16,363 --> 00:47:22,363
was produced in lieu of an abbreviated,
six-episode sixth season requested by MTV.

17
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
Series co-creator Glenn Eichler planned to wrap the show with the fifth-season
finale "Boxing Daria", believing that there was no more story to tell.

18
00:53:10,909 --> 00:53:16,909
The film was first broadcast by MTV on January 21, 2002, released on both VHS and DVD formats on August 27,
2002, and was included on the DVD release of Daria: The Complete Animated Series on May 11, 2010.

19
00:56:08,181 --> 00:56:14,181
The film has yet to see a Blu-ray release.

20
00:59:05,454 --> 00:59:11,454
The film explores themes of high school, college,
graduation, misanthrophy, high school graduation.

21
